      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- FCLT_ROOMS\n- FCLT_BUILDING\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- geometric mean of the total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- subjects offered: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- regular terms: ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM\n- total units greater than zero: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- academic building: FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE, FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_NAME\n- building name: FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_NAME\n- rooms larger than 40 square meters: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- room area: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- average of the room areas: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- range of the room areas: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- variance of the room areas: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA\n- total assignable area of the building: FCLT_BUILDING.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\n- year the building was built: FCLT_BUILDING.DATE_BUILT\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\n- FCLT_BUILDING.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <-> FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each academic year, what is the academic year description and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered in terms that are regular terms and have total units greater than zero?\n```sql\nSELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, EXP(AVG(LN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS))) AS geometric_mean_total_units FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE WHERE ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' AND COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC ORDER BY geometric_mean_total_units DESC;\n```\n2. For each building, give the building name and calculate the average, range, and variance of the room areas for rooms in that building where the building type is 'ACADEMIC' and the room area is greater than 40.\n```sql\nSELECT b.BUILDING_NAME, AVG(r.AREA) AS avg_room_area, MAX(r.AREA) - MIN(r.AREA) AS room_area_range, VARIANCE(r.AREA) AS room_area_variance FROM FCLT_ROOMS r JOIN FCLT_BUILDING b ON r.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE b.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND r.AREA > 40 GROUP BY b.BUILDING_NAME ORDER BY room_area_range DESC;\n```\n3. Show the department names, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by each department in regular terms with total units greater than zero.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, EXP(AVG(LN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS))) AS geometric_mean_total_units, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE WHERE ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' AND COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, inner_cte.ACADEMIC_YEAR, inner_cte.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, inner_cte.geometric_mean_total_units FROM inner_cte ORDER BY inner_cte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, inner_cte.ACADEMIC_YEAR DESC;\n```\n4. For each academic building with rooms larger than 40 square meters, show the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, and also display the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT b.BUILDING_NAME, AVG(r.AREA) AS avg_room_area, MAX(r.AREA) - MIN(r.AREA) AS room_area_range, VARIANCE(r.AREA) AS room_area_variance FROM FCLT_ROOMS r JOIN FCLT_BUILDING b ON r.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY WHERE b.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND r.AREA > 40 GROUP BY b.BUILDING_NAME ) SELECT ic.BUILDING_NAME, ic.avg_room_area, ic.room_area_range, ic.room_area_variance, fb.ASSIGNABLE_AREA, fb.DATE_BUILT FROM inner_cte ic JOIN FCLT_BUILDING fb ON ic.BUILDING_NAME = fb.BUILDING_NAME ORDER BY ic.room_area_range DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers."
