    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is unavailable (access denied on every attempt, including `SELECT 1`), so I cannot execute verification queries. However, the semantic network contains an **exact precedent metric `dw_4061`** whose description matches the question word-for-word, with full SQL retrieved via `semantic_get`. The hint-provided gold tables, column mapping, join keys, and subquery decomposition all corroborate this precedent. I'll produce the report and final SQL based on this evidence.\n\n---\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (core):**\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Academic term dimension, one row per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE` (YYYYTT), `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM` ('Y'/'N' — regular = Fall/Spring; only present here, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL).\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Catalog-level subject offering, one row per subject offering per term/academic year. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` (term from which catalog attributes take effect — the documented join to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering), `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `MEET_PLACE` (stores the FCLT room key; joins to FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY).\n- **FCLT_ROOMS** — Facilities room inventory, one row per room. Key columns: `FCLT_ROOM_KEY`, `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY`, `AREA` (square meters; documented for average/range/variance statistics).\n- **FCLT_BUILDING** — Facilities building inventory, one row per building. Key columns: `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY`, `BUILDING_NAME`, `BUILDING_TYPE` ('ACADEMIC'/'SERVICE'/'RESIDENT'), `ASSIGNABLE_AREA` (total assignable area, sq m), `DATE_BUILT` (MM/DD/YYYY; year built derived from it).\n\n**Tables (peripheral, investigated/discarded):** SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED (registrar-side unit/enrollment facts — no MEET_PLACE room-key link documented to FCLT_ROOMS at catalog grain, and the question's \"subjects offered\" maps to the catalog per hint column mapping); ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (lacks IS_REGULAR_TERM — VIOLATES the \"regular terms\" filter); FCLT_BUILDING_HIST / FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 (per-fiscal-period history — question asks current building attributes); FAC_BUILDING / FAC_ROOMS (FAC_* key family, not linked to FCLT_ROOMS keys); SPACE_DETAIL / BUILDINGS (square feet, space-assignment perspective); FCLT_FLOOR (floor grain, not needed); SIS_DEPARTMENT / STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (department dimension — question needs only DEPARTMENT_NAME which exists directly on the catalog table); CIS_COURSE_CATALOG / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG (alternative catalog feeds; hint mapping anchors to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED).\n\n**Metric:** `dw_4061` — \"Department Geometric Mean Total Units with Academic Building Room Area Statistics\" — description is **identical** to the question; full SQL retrieved (see Section 6).\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_total_units` (decision guide: \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/**geometric mean**) over catalog offerings → Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\"); `column_concept_department_name` (catalog filtering → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME); `column_concept_year_columns` (term-status filters → join ACADEMIC_TERMS); `column_concept_assignable_area` (\"Total assignable area of a building (current) → FCLT_BUILDING.ASSIGNABLE_AREA\"); `column_concept_building_type_site` (\"current academic buildings → FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE, one row per building, no period duplication\").\n\n**Concepts:** concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_building_inventory, concept_room_space_inventory — group the candidates above; their decision guides consistently point to the four gold tables for this task shape.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS (joins edge; TERM_CODE / EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED → FCLT_ROOMS (joins edge; MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOM_KEY, documented in both table descriptions).\n- FCLT_ROOMS → FCLT_BUILDING (joins edge; FCLT_BUILDING_KEY, parent/child).\n- dw_4061 lineage: ACADEMIC_TERMS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_BUILDING — exactly the four gold tables.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (unit-source candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | per subject offering per term/year (table desc) | per subject (cluster) per term (table desc) | per term (table desc) |\n| MEET_PLACE room key | YES — joins FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY (column def) | not documented | n/a |\n| IS_REGULAR_TERM filter | via ACADEMIC_TERMS join | via ACADEMIC_TERMS join | NOT-SUPPORTED (column absent per desc) |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | yes | yes | n/a |\n\n**Building candidates:** FCLT_BUILDING (current, one row/building) vs FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (per-fiscal-period rows → row multiplication, per column_concept_building_type_site comparison) vs FAC_BUILDING (different key family) vs BUILDINGS (square feet, no BUILDING_TYPE).\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- \"regular terms\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM: SUPPORTED (only ACADEMIC_TERMS carries it); ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: VIOLATES.\n- \"geometric mean of total units\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS: SUPPORTED (decision guide explicitly names geometric mean).\n- \"academic building where these subjects are held\" → requires MEET_PLACE→FCLT_ROOM_KEY link: SUPPORTED only by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED among unit tables.\n- \"rooms larger than 40 sq meters\" → FCLT_ROOMS.AREA (sq m per column def): SUPPORTED; SPACE_DETAIL/BUILDINGS are sq ft: VIOLATES unit semantics.\n- \"total assignable area / year built\" → FCLT_BUILDING.ASSIGNABLE_AREA / DATE_BUILT: SUPPORTED (decision guide: current building total).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"department name\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME (hint mapping + column_concept decision guide); \"academic year description\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC; \"academic building\" → FCLT_BUILDING.BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC' + BUILDING_NAME; \"where these subjects are held\" → MEET_PLACE join. All anchors are unique — no ambiguity remains.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Exact-shape precedent: 1 — dw_4061 (identical question text, full SQL on the four gold tables). Related geometric-mean precedents on ACADEMIC_TERMS + catalog: dw_4701, dw_2957. Building room-area stats precedents on FCLT_ROOMS/FCLT_BUILDING: dw_488, dw_1488, dw_1190, dw_1888, dw_3332.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: consumed by dozens of unit-statistics metrics (dw_41, dw_1023, dw_2597, dw_3417, dw_4061…); serves \"units by department/year/term-status\" question patterns; its MEET_PLACE column is the documented bridge to facilities analysis.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS: the standard term-status filter dimension (IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR) across offering metrics.\n- FCLT_ROOMS/FCLT_BUILDING: standard pair for room-area dispersion statistics per building (dw_488, dw_1190, dw_1488, dw_1888).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- dw_4061: semantic_get ✓ (full SQL). ACADEMIC_TERMS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_BUILDING: semantic_get ✓ + semantic_graph neighbors ✓ (CCSO, FCLT_ROOMS). column_concept_total_units / department_name / year_columns / assignable_area / building_type_site: semantic_get ✓. Concepts (subject_offering_facts, academic_term_dimension, building_inventory, room_space_inventory, course_catalog_sources, department_dimension): retrieved via search descs; membership evidence used in 3a/3b. Peripheral tables (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST(_1), FAC_*, SPACE_DETAIL, BUILDINGS, FCLT_FLOOR, SIS/STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, CIS/DRUPAL catalogs): investigated via search descs + concept comparisons; excluded with reasons in §1/§3. Related metrics (dw_2597, dw_3417, dw_41, dw_1023, dw_488, dw_1488, dw_1190, dw_1888, dw_505, dw_1357, dw_3332, dw_1833, dw_4701, dw_2957): descs reviewed as precedent evidence. mysql_query: attempted 3× — database access denied (environment issue), noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use the four gold tables: ACADEMIC_TERMS (IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y', ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (DEPARTMENT_NAME, TOTAL_UNITS, EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE, MEET_PLACE), FCLT_ROOMS (AREA, FCLT_ROOM_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING_KEY), FCLT_BUILDING (BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC', BUILDING_NAME, ASSIGNABLE_AREA, DATE_BUILT).\n\n**6b.** Two CTEs + bridge join, following the dw_4061 precedent exactly:\n1. `dept_units`: geometric mean `EXP(AVG(LN(TOTAL_UNITS)))` per (ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME), joining ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE, filtering IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' AND TOTAL_UNITS>0.\n2. `building_stats`: AVG / MAX−MIN / VARIANCE of room AREA per BUILDING_NAME for ACADEMIC buildings with AREA>40.\n3. Final: re-join `dept_units` to catalog rows (DEPARTMENT_NAME + ACADEMIC_YEAR) to find where those subjects are held via MEET_PLACE=FCLT_ROOM_KEY → FCLT_BUILDING → building_stats (BUILDING_NAME), attaching ASSIGNABLE_AREA and DATE_BUILT. ORDER BY department name, academic year DESC, room area range DESC. No rounding.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: MEET_PLACE stores the FCLT room key (column def); AREA is sq m matching \"40 square meters\"; FCLT_BUILDING is one row per building (no fan-out on ASSIGNABLE_AREA/DATE_BUILT). *Semantic-network*: dw_4061 lineage covers exactly these four tables; column-concept decision guides anchor every measure/filter column. *Business*: identical-question precedent dw_4061 provides the exact SQL; room-area dispersion precedents (dw_488/1190/1488) use the same FCLT_ROOMS⋈FCLT_BUILDING pattern with VARIANCE/MAX−MIN.\n\n**6d.** No tie-breakers needed — the exact-shape precedent is unambiguous. Caveat: mysql verification was impossible (DB access denied); the SQL is taken verbatim from the stored precedent metric, which is the authoritative gold SQL.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_8f947580c7c34d5c95abe086",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH dept_units AS (\\n  SELECT ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n         ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC,\\n         EXP(AVG(LN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS))) AS geometric_mean_total_units,\\n         COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n  FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS\\n  JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\\n    ON ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\\n  WHERE ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'\\n    AND COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS > 0\\n  GROUP BY ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n), building_stats AS (\\n  SELECT b.BUILDING_NAME,\\n         AVG(r.AREA) AS avg_room_area,\\n         MAX(r.AREA) - MIN(r.AREA) AS room_area_range,\\n         VARIANCE(r.AREA) AS room_area_variance\\n  FROM FCLT_ROOMS r\\n  JOIN FCLT_BUILDING b ON r.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\\n  WHERE b.BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC' AND r.AREA > 40\\n  GROUP BY b.BUILDING_NAME\\n)\\nSELECT ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       ds.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n       ds.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC,\\n       ds.geometric_mean_total_units,\\n       bs.BUILDING_NAME,\\n       bs.avg_room_area,\\n       bs.room_area_range,\\n       bs.room_area_variance,\\n       fb.ASSIGNABLE_AREA,\\n       fb.DATE_BUILT\\nFROM dept_units ds\\nJOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED cso\\n  ON ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME = cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n AND ds.ACADEMIC_YEAR = cso.ACADEMIC_YEAR\\nJOIN FCLT_ROOMS fr ON cso.MEET_PLACE = fr.FCLT_ROOM_KEY\\nJOIN FCLT_BUILDING fb ON fr.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = fb.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY\\nJOIN building_stats bs ON fb.BUILDING_NAME = bs.BUILDING_NAME\\nORDER BY ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ds.ACADEMIC_YEAR DESC, bs.room_area_range DESC;\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
